      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "The promising BASSETT BABE (5) returns and has found a nice race to kick things off on the right note. Made quite the impression in her debut prep and is destined to be tackling black type again soon. Fitted with a jumpout and is clearly the one to beat. ANGEL TORQUE (3) is another handy one resuming and is a noted winner. Shoulders peaks that are competitive and has been readied with two sharp jumpouts, though is unexposed on a heavy deck. MIC DROP (1) progressed through her grades rapidly last prep and if she's come on again through the break she deserves serious consideration. Any late money will be key. DEEPFLOAT DIVA (4) has been frustrating for his supporters this prep but has peaks that can see him in the finish. RAIKOKE (2) was too bad to be true last start but his prior form reads strongly. Could sprint well off 45 days in-between.",
